# Cloudflare Pages sets NODE_ENV=production as a build environment variable
# (visible in the build log's "Build environment variables" section, coming
# from wrangler.toml's vars / the Pages project settings — not something
# this repo's build step sets itself). With NODE_ENV=production present in
# the environment, `npm ci` silently omits devDependencies — verified by
# reproducing the exact failure locally: `NODE_ENV=production npm ci`
# installs ~123 packages instead of the full ~360+, and everything under
# devDependencies (@sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare, @sveltejs/kit, vite,
# tailwindcss, postcss, typescript, svelte-check, ...) goes missing, which
# is exactly what broke the Cloudflare Pages build ("Cannot find module
# @sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare imported from svelte.config.js"). Those are
# all build-time-only tools with no runtime footprint, but the build itself
# cannot run without them. `omit=` (empty) forces npm to install every
# dependency class regardless of NODE_ENV.
omit=
